<title>MEXICO: Mexico auto production hits new record.</title>
<headline>Mexico auto production hits new record.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican auto production for the first 11 months of the year was a record 1,138,818 units, the Mexican Automobile Industry Association (AMIA) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The previous record production level for the first 11 months was in 1994, when 1,097,381 vehicles were made, the AMIA said in a statement.  </p>
<p>Production for export during the January-November period was 901,873 units, up 26.2 percent compared to the same period of 1995.</p>
<p>The AMIA said that despite the record in overall production, domestic sales were still lagging 1994 levels. Still, it added, &quot;there is evidence of a steady recovery.&quot;</p>
